#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""guard_promotion.py - PreToolUse hook: a PROMOTION write must carry its honest label.

Enforces the campaign's #1 hard gate on every promotion surface. A current-best pointer carries the
label its checks earned; a FINDING - POSITIVE or NEGATIVE (steering-negatives promote too) -
promoted upward may not be unless an independent check recorded a promotable verdict artifact in
results/verdicts/<id>.json:
    {"claim": "...", "exp_id": "...", "verdict": "CONFIRMED", "kill_tier": null,
     "refuter": "<agent/session id>", "utc": "...", "summary": "..."}
For a NEGATIVE (kill-claim) finding, "kill_tier" is "REFUTED" or "EVIDENCE_AGAINST" (an "INCONCLUSIVE"
kill never graduates - it queues a fix-and-rerun unit instead).

Two promotion surfaces, two strictness tiers. The citation rule and the surface/recency rule are
independent and complementary - a write must satisfy both, not either:
  * RECOMMENDED*.json (current-best) writes and scoreboard writes that INTRODUCE a `CONFIRMED` /
    `NEW BEST` token - SUBJECT-MATCHED + FAIL-OPEN-LOGGED: the pointer follows the true best at once
   , so the write must carry the promoted experiment's HONEST LABEL - exactly the one its
    checks artifact holds (results/checks_<NN>.json `label`: unverified, self-checked, self-verified,
    <VERDICT>/peer, <VERDICT>/verifier), never a stronger one - and a result a check refuted never
    promotes. An experiment whose checks artifact predates the one-check rule (no `verification.owed`)
    keeps the established rule: the verdict artifact FOR THAT EXPERIMENT (matched by the exp id/name the written content carries) must
    be CONFIRMED with a NAMED INDEPENDENT REFUTER and a graduating kill tier if any. These files are
    recoverable, so a guard *error* here allows BUT logs to results/gate_failures.log (campaign-status
    hard-fails on a non-empty log); a wrong label or an unmatched verdict is a clean, recoverable DENY.
  * the PROJECT ledger <project>/DISCOVERIES.md - SUBJECT-MATCHED + FAIL-CLOSED: promoting a
    system-level finding upward must cite the SOURCE campaign's verdict artifact by name
    (campaigns/<slug>/results/verdicts/<id>.json); the artifact must be CONFIRMED with a named refuter
    and a graduating kill tier, and the source campaign's correctness suite must be an affirmative,
    non-stale GREEN. Any guard error on this surface DENIES - the project ledger is the record that
    survives fork-and-archive, the one unrecoverable write.
The campaign surface also requires an AFFIRMATIVE GREEN correctness suite (results/correctness_state.json,
written by run_campaign) - not merely 'not red'. RED, EMPTY (a freshly-scaffolded all-skip suite: zero
active checks), ERROR, ABSENT, and a never-run (no state file) all block, because none is evidence the
machinery is right - deleting/never-finishing the suite was the trivial silent bypass. ABSENT/EMPTY are
excused only by an explicit tests/CORRECTNESS_NA.md (a recorded N/A decision, never a silent gap). A green
is further rejected if STALE - recorded against a different FROZEN/core hash than the code on disk (the
file set is scripts/frozen_core.py). No finding built on a red/empty/absent suite, or on a green that no
longer matches the code it certified, is trustworthy.

Settled findings are RECORDED as the ledger's `finding` cells (results/scoreboard.tsv), written by the
runner through `--record <exp> --finding`, each citing its verdict; results/JOURNAL.md is working
memory, edited every cycle, and is deliberately NOT a gated surface: the mechanical authorities
downstream trusts are the scoreboard's verified column and RECOMMENDED.json, which are. A finding cell
with no verdict citation is an open question, not a finding; campaign-status audits that.

A normal scoreboard row append (no promotion token) is recording, not promotion - never gated. Writes
to anything else are always allowed; unparseable stdin is allowed + logged (we cannot even tell what is
being written).

One further surface serves the metric-epoch design, keyed on PHYSKIT_ROLE - the marker the driver sets
in every spawned role's environment; an ATTENDED session (the user, or run-campaign on the user's word)
has none. It is configs/loop.json, and it carries two rules:
  * the `campaign.metric_revision` dial (who may revise the FROZEN metric) may not be moved by a spawned
    role. Every other knob passes for everyone. Fail-open-logged.
  * `campaign.metric_epochs` - the metric-epoch record, keyed by metric_version, present only once a
    campaign has revised its metric (the first epoch is implicit) - is APPEND-ONLY (kind and evidence never
    change, no entry is removed); a new entry carries its evidence (a semantics epoch cites a CONFIRMED
    kill verdict against the old metric with a graduating tier - REFUTED only for an 'easier' ruler; a
    mechanics epoch names its reproducing check); a spawned role may add one only when the dial delegates
    it, and only as 'pending'; a standing change (pending -> ratified | rolled-back) is the user's, from an
    attended session, and a resolved epoch is final. FAIL-CLOSED for the block - every epoch label rests
    on it. The scorer hash an epoch is bound to is the runner's (results/correctness_state.json).
  * A promotion (surface 2) additionally requires the current metric_version to be a declared (or the
    implicit first), non-rolled-back epoch; a PENDING epoch promotes (promote-and-label: the row carries its
    metric_version, the declaration the standing).

SCOPE (gaps campaign-status backstops): the scoreboard signal is token-based - a promotion phrased
without those tokens slips past (verified-column check is the backstop); the hook only fires if THIS
tree wired it (.claude/settings.json) - campaign-status asserts the wiring - and it is wired per
CAMPAIGN, so a session rooted at the project level writes the project ledger unhooked (the promotion
path runs from inside a campaign, where it is hooked).
"""
from __future__ import annotations
import json
import os
import re
import sys
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path

VERDICT_REF_RE = re.compile(r"verdicts[/\\]([\w\-.]+\.json)")
SUBJECT_RE = re.compile(r"exp[\w\-]*\d[\w\-]*", re.I)
PROMOTABLE = {"CONFIRMED"}
# metric epochs + the metric_revision dial (the metric-epoch design)
EPOCH_KINDS = {"mechanics", "semantics"}
EPOCH_STATUSES = {"pending", "ratified", "rolled-back"}
EPOCH_DIRECTIONS = {"harder", "easier", "neutral"}
ROLE_ENV = "PHYSKIT_ROLE"       # set by the driver for every spawned role; absent = an attended session


def _allow():
    sys.exit(0)


_LOG_ROOT = None   # the campaign root of the file being written, set by main() once it is known


def _log_denial(reason: str) -> None:
    """Every denial lands in results/guard_denials.log - the count that decides whether this hook earns
    its keep (a guard that never denies is either a deterrent or dead weight; only the log can tell)."""
    root = _LOG_ROOT or _env_campaign_root()
    if root is None:
        return
    try:
        log = root / "results" / "guard_denials.log"
        log.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with open(log, "a", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            f.write(f"{datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()}\tDENY\t{reason[:300]}\n")
    except Exception:
        pass


def _deny(reason: str):
    _log_denial(reason)
    print(json.dumps({"hookSpecificOutput": {
        "hookEventName": "PreToolUse",
        "permissionDecision": "deny",
        "permissionDecisionReason": reason,
    }}))
    sys.exit(0)


def _campaign_root(fp: Path) -> Path | None:
    """The dir holding scripts/ + configs/, walking up from the written file."""
    for parent in fp.parents:
        if (parent / "scripts").is_dir() and (parent / "configs").is_dir():
            return parent
    return None


def _env_campaign_root() -> Path | None:
    """The campaign root from CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, which Claude Code sets to the tree that wired this hook.

    Used when the written path cannot resolve a root (the unparseable-stdin fail-open has no path at all).
    """
    d = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR", "").strip()
    if not d:
        return None
    p = Path(d)
    return p if (p / "scripts").is_dir() and (p / "configs").is_dir() else None


def _is_project_ledger(fp: Path | None) -> bool:
    """True for the PROJECT-level `DISCOVERIES*.md` - basename-matched, parent must BE a project root
    (PROJECT.md beside the written file; LINEAGE.md is NOT required, because the consolidated layout
    absorbed it into PROJECT.md).

    New projects no longer scaffold a DISCOVERIES ledger at all (findings live
    in the campaign that produced them, pointed at from PROJECT.md §Lineage / §Updates from
    discoveries). This surface stays so a LEGACY or imported ledger remains gated rather than
    silently fail-open - and detection must therefore not key on LINEAGE.md, which a consolidated
    project holding an imported old ledger will not have.

    The campaign-level results*/DISCOVERIES.md surface this hook once guarded no longer exists: settled
    findings live in the ledger's `finding` cells (runner-written), and the file dissolved (V6). What remains
    ledger-shaped is the project record, which the old guard could never validate (its `_campaign_root`
    cannot resolve above a campaign, so every project-level write hit an unsatisfiable deny). This
    predicate knows about project roots, closing that deliberately deferred gap.
    """
    if fp is None or not fp.name.upper().endswith(".MD"):
        return False
    if not fp.name.upper().startswith("DISCOVERIES"):
        return False
    parent = fp.parent
    try:
        return (parent / "PROJECT.md").is_file()
    except OSError:
        return False


def _find_project_verdict(project_root: Path, name: str) -> Path | None:
    """The cited verdict artifact anywhere under the project's campaigns (incl. campaigns/_archive)."""
    hits = sorted(project_root.glob(f"campaigns/**/verdicts/{name}"))
    return hits[0] if hits else None


def _spawned_role() -> str:
    return os.environ.get(ROLE_ENV, "").strip().lower()


def _new_full_text(fp: Path | None, ti) -> str | None:
    """The file's content AFTER this Write / Edit / MultiEdit, reconstructed from the on-disk text. None if
    it cannot be (an old_string that is not in the file, or an unreadable file)."""
    if ti.get("content") is not None:
        return str(ti.get("content", ""))
    try:
        text = fp.read_text(encoding="utf-8") if (fp is not None and fp.is_file()) else ""
    except OSError:
        return None
    edits = []
    if ti.get("new_string") is not None:
        edits.append((str(ti.get("old_string", "") or ""), str(ti.get("new_string", "")),
                      bool(ti.get("replace_all"))))
    for e in (ti.get("edits") or []):
        if isinstance(e, dict):
            edits.append((str(e.get("old_string", "") or ""), str(e.get("new_string", "")),
                          bool(e.get("replace_all"))))
    for old, new, everywhere in edits:
        if not old or old not in text:
            return None
        text = text.replace(old, new) if everywhere else text.replace(old, new, 1)
    return text


def _campaign_key(text: str, key: str, default=None):
    """configs/loop.json text -> campaign.<key> (or default); "__unparseable__" if the text is not JSON."""
    try:
        d = json.loads(text) if text else {}
    except Exception:
        return "__unparseable__"
    camp = d.get("campaign") if isinstance(d, dict) else None
    return camp.get(key, default) if isinstance(camp, dict) else default


def _loop_campaign_key(root: Path | None, key: str, default=None):
    if root is None:
        return default
    try:
        v = _campaign_key((root / "configs" / "loop.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"), key, default)
    except Exception:
        return default
    return default if v == "__unparseable__" else v


def _is_loop_config(fp: Path | None) -> bool:
    return (fp is not None and fp.name.lower() == "loop.json"
            and fp.parent.name.lower().startswith("configs"))


def config_dial_problem(fp: Path, ti) -> str | None:
    """Deny-reason if a DRIVER-SPAWNED role is moving campaign.metric_revision, else None.

    The dial says who may revise the FROZEN metric, so it is the one config key an agent must not set for
    itself: it is the user's decision, made from an attended session (the metric-epoch rules). Attended sessions
    (no PHYSKIT_ROLE) pass; every other loop.json knob passes for everyone."""
    role = _spawned_role()
    if not role:
        return None
    new_text = _new_full_text(fp, ti)
    if new_text is None:
        return None
    new_val = _campaign_key(new_text, "metric_revision")
    if new_val == "__unparseable__":
        return None                    # not a provable flip; the runner refuses a broken loop.json anyway
    try:
        old_text = fp.read_text(encoding="utf-8") if fp.is_file() else ""
    except OSError:
        old_text = ""
    old_val = _campaign_key(old_text, "metric_revision")

    def norm(v):
        return "cautious" if v == "__unparseable__" else str(v or "cautious").strip().lower()

    if norm(new_val) != norm(old_val):
        return (f"config gate: a driver-spawned {role} may not change campaign.metric_revision "
                f"({norm(old_val)!r} -> {norm(new_val)!r}). That dial is the USER's decision (the metric-epoch design): it "
                "is set from an attended session - the user editing configs/loop.json, run-campaign on their "
                "request, or `run_campaign.py --set-metric-revision`. If you believe the mode should change, "
                "say so in results/ESCALATE.md or the journal and leave the file alone.")
    return None


def _kill_tier(v: dict) -> str:
    return str(v.get("kill_tier") or "").strip().upper().replace(" ", "_").replace("-", "_")


def _epoch_evidence_problem(root: Path | None, entry: dict) -> str | None:
    """The evidence rule for a NEW epoch entry (the metric-epoch evidence rule): a semantics epoch cites a CONFIRMED kill
    verdict against the current metric with a graduating tier - REFUTED or EVIDENCE_AGAINST, and REFUTED
    only when the revision is 'easier' (the goalpost-moving shape); a mechanics epoch names the check that
    reproduced the discrepancy. An epoch with no evidence is a metric change nobody verified."""
    kind = str(entry.get("kind", ""))
    ev = str(entry.get("evidence") or "").strip()
    eid = entry.get("id")
    if kind == "mechanics":
        if not ev:
            return (f"epoch {eid!r} (mechanics) names no evidence - record the correctness check that "
                    "reproduces the discrepancy on the old scorer and passes on the new one")
        return None
    direction = str(entry.get("expected_direction") or "").strip().lower()
    if direction not in EPOCH_DIRECTIONS:
        return (f"epoch {eid!r} (semantics) must declare expected_direction: "
                + " | ".join(sorted(EPOCH_DIRECTIONS)))
    m = VERDICT_REF_RE.search(ev)
    if not m:
        return (f"epoch {eid!r} (semantics) cites no verdict artifact - a metric revision needs the verify "
                "skill's kill verdict against the CURRENT metric (results/verdicts/<id>.json) before it can "
                "open an epoch; an unverified 'the metric is flawed' is exactly the claim this gate exists "
                "to check")
    if root is None:
        return "cannot resolve the campaign root to find the cited verdict"
    path = root / "results" / "verdicts" / m.group(1)
    if not path.is_file():
        return f"epoch {eid!r}: cited verdict artifact not found: results/verdicts/{m.group(1)}"
    try:
        reason = _check_verdict(path, m.group(1))
        v = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except Exception as exc:
        return f"epoch {eid!r}: cited verdict artifact unreadable ({exc})"
    if reason:
        return f"epoch {eid!r}: {reason}"
    tier = _kill_tier(v)
    if not tier:
        return (f"epoch {eid!r}: verdicts/{m.group(1)} carries no kill_tier - a metric revision rests on a "
                "verified KILL of the old metric (kill_tier REFUTED or EVIDENCE_AGAINST), not on a "
                "confirmation of a result")
    if direction == "easier" and tier != "REFUTED":
        return (f"epoch {eid!r} is an EASIER ruler (the current best would score better) and its kill "
                f"verdict is only {tier} - an easier-ruler revision needs a REFUTED-tier kill of the old "
                "metric (the metric-epoch evidence rule); weaker evidence goes to the user via results/ESCALATE.md")
    return None


def _epoch_block(text: str):
    """campaign.metric_epochs from loop.json text: a dict (absent = {}), or "__unparseable__"."""
    v = _campaign_key(text, "metric_epochs", None)
    if v == "__unparseable__":
        return v
    return v if isinstance(v, dict) else ({} if v is None else "__not_an_object__")


def epoch_block_problem(root: Path | None, fp: Path, ti) -> str | None:
    """Deny-reason for a configs/loop.json write that breaks campaign.metric_epochs' contract, else None.

    The block is the metric-epoch record and is append-only: an entry's kind and evidence never change and
    no entry is removed. A new entry carries its evidence (_epoch_evidence_problem) and, from a spawned
    role, is allowed only when the campaign's metric_revision dial delegates it, always as 'pending'.
    Standing changes (pending -> ratified | rolled-back) are the USER's: attended sessions only, and a
    resolved epoch is final. FAIL-CLOSED for the block - every epoch label rests on it. A write that does
    not involve the block at all passes (the dial check is separate)."""
    role = _spawned_role()
    try:
        old_text = fp.read_text(encoding="utf-8") if fp.is_file() else ""
    except OSError:
        old_text = ""
    # Involvement is the quoted JSON KEY, not the bare word: the campaign block's own _doc string names
    # metric_epochs in prose, and an edit that never touches the block must not be judged by it.
    if '"metric_epochs"' not in _written_text(ti) and '"metric_epochs"' not in old_text:
        return None
    new_text = _new_full_text(fp, ti)
    if new_text is None:
        return ("cannot reconstruct the loop.json this edit produces (an old_string not present in the "
                "file?) - rewrite the campaign block whole so the gate can check metric_epochs")
    new_block = _epoch_block(new_text)
    if new_block == "__unparseable__":
        return "the write leaves configs/loop.json unparseable"
    if new_block == "__not_an_object__":
        return "campaign.metric_epochs must be a JSON object keyed by metric_version"
    old_block = _epoch_block(old_text)
    if not isinstance(old_block, dict):
        if role:
            return ("the loop.json on disk is unreadable and a spawned role may not rewrite its epoch block "
                    "- an attended session repairs it")
        old_block = {}
    mode = _campaign_key(old_text, "metric_revision", "cautious")
    mode = "cautious" if mode == "__unparseable__" else str(mode or "cautious").strip().lower()
    for vid, e in new_block.items():
        vid = str(vid).strip()
        if not vid or not isinstance(e, dict):
            return "every metric_epochs entry is keyed by a non-empty metric_version and is an object"
        kind, status = str(e.get("kind", "")), str(e.get("status", ""))
        if kind not in EPOCH_KINDS:
            return f"epoch {vid!r}: kind must be " + " | ".join(sorted(EPOCH_KINDS))
        if status not in EPOCH_STATUSES:
            return f"epoch {vid!r}: status must be " + " | ".join(sorted(EPOCH_STATUSES))
        prior = old_block.get(vid)
        if isinstance(prior, dict):
            if str(prior.get("kind", "")) != kind:
                return f"epoch {vid!r}: kind is append-only ({prior.get('kind')!r} -> {kind!r})"
            if (prior.get("evidence") or None) != (e.get("evidence") or None):
                return f"epoch {vid!r}: evidence is append-only; open a new epoch for a new justification"
            old_status = str(prior.get("status", ""))
            if old_status != status:
                if role:
                    return (f"epoch {vid!r}: {old_status} -> {status} is a RATIFICATION decision, and a "
                            f"driver-spawned {role} may not make it. Ratification is the user's: it happens "
                            "from an attended session (run-campaign relays it on the user's word). Leave "
                            "the status 'pending' and surface the epoch in the journal.")
                if old_status != "pending":
                    return (f"epoch {vid!r}: a {old_status} epoch is final ({old_status} -> {status}); "
                            "record a reversal as a NEW epoch, never by rewriting standing")
            continue
        # a NEW entry
        if role:
            if mode != "autonomous":
                return (f"epoch {vid!r}: campaign.metric_revision is {mode!r}, so a driver-spawned {role} "
                        "may not open a metric epoch. Propose it instead: write results/ESCALATE.md (the "
                        "claim, the verdict, the proposed change, its expected_direction) and the user "
                        "opens the epoch.")
            if status != "pending":
                return (f"epoch {vid!r}: a spawned role opens an epoch as 'pending' (this one was written "
                        f"{status!r}); ratification is the user's")
        problem = _epoch_evidence_problem(root, dict(e, id=vid))
        if problem:
            return problem
    removed = sorted(set(old_block) - {str(k).strip() for k in new_block})
    if removed:
        return ("metric_epochs is append-only; this write removes epoch(s) " + ", ".join(removed)
                + " - roll an epoch back by setting its status, never by deleting it")
    return None


def epoch_blocks_promotion(root: Path | None) -> str | None:
    """Deny-reason if the CURRENT metric epoch cannot carry a promotion, else None. A PENDING epoch
    promotes (promote-and-label: the row carries its metric_version, the declaration carries the standing);
    a rolled-back one, or a metric_version the block never declared, does not. No block = the implicit
    first epoch = pass."""
    if root is None:
        return None
    mv = str(_loop_campaign_key(root, "metric_version", "") or "").strip()
    block = _loop_campaign_key(root, "metric_epochs", None)
    if not mv or not isinstance(block, dict) or not block:
        return None
    cur = block.get(mv)
    if not isinstance(cur, dict):
        # The first epoch never needs an entry: it is the one version the runner could bind before any
        # block existed. Anything else absent from the block is an undeclared bump.
        st = _read_correctness(root) or {}
        if (st.get("scorer_hash_by_version") or {}).get(mv):
            return None
        return (f"campaign.metric_version {mv!r} is not declared in campaign.metric_epochs (declared: "
                f"{', '.join(str(k) for k in block) or 'none'}) - a metric_version bump is an epoch; declare "
                "it (with its evidence) before promoting anything scored under it")
    if str(cur.get("status", "")) == "rolled-back":
        return (f"the current metric epoch {mv!r} is ROLLED-BACK - nothing scored under it promotes. Point "
                "campaign.metric_version at the epoch the campaign reverted to, or open the next epoch")
    return None


def _note_bypass(root: Path | None, reason: str):
    """Fail-open must never be silent: record it so campaign-status can hard-fail on it.

    The record MUST land in the campaign that was bypassed. It used to fall back to Path(".") -- the
    process's cwd -- so a bypass with no resolvable root wrote results/gate_failures.log wherever the hook
    happened to be invoked from. campaign-status reads that log INSIDE the campaign, so the one path built
    to keep a fail-open non-silent was the path that could silence it; worse, the stray log makes an
    UNRELATED tree hard-fail on a bypass that never concerned it. So: resolve from CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR
    before giving up, and if no campaign root can be established, write nothing and say so on stderr.
    """
    root = root or _env_campaign_root()
    if root is None:
        print(f"guard_promotion FAIL-OPEN (no campaign root; not logged): {reason}", file=sys.stderr)
        return
    try:
        log = root / "results" / "gate_failures.log"
        log.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with open(log, "a", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            f.write(f"{datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()}\tFAIL-OPEN\t{reason}\n")
    except Exception:
        pass


def _edit_chunks(ti):
    """Yield (new_text, old_text) pairs a Write / Edit / MultiEdit introduces."""
    if ti.get("content") is not None:
        yield str(ti.get("content", "")), ""
    if ti.get("new_string") is not None:
        yield str(ti.get("new_string", "")), str(ti.get("old_string", "") or "")
    for e in (ti.get("edits") or []):
        if isinstance(e, dict):
            yield str(e.get("new_string", "")), str(e.get("old_string", "") or "")


def _written_text(ti) -> str:
    return "\n".join(new for new, _ in _edit_chunks(ti))


def _read_correctness(root: Path | None) -> dict | None:
    """The recorded correctness-suite state dict, or None if there is no readable state file."""
    if root is None:
        return None
    state = root / "results" / "correctness_state.json"
    if not state.is_file():
        return None
    try:
        return json.loads(state.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except Exception:
        return None


def _has_na_waiver(root: Path | None) -> bool:
    """A recorded N/A decision: tests/CORRECTNESS_NA.md exists with a non-empty rationale. It excuses ONLY an
    ABSENT or EMPTY suite (a campaign with genuinely no simulator to check) - never RED/ERROR (a real or
    broken suite). Making the gap an explicit, reviewable file is the point: it kills the SILENT bypass
    (delete/never-build the suite), not the possibility of a deliberate, recorded N/A."""
    if root is None:
        return False
    w = root / "tests" / "CORRECTNESS_NA.md"
    try:
        return w.is_file() and bool(w.read_text(encoding="utf-8").strip())
    except Exception:
        return False


def correctness_blocks_promotion(root: Path | None, relaxed: bool = False) -> str | None:
    """Deny-reason if the correctness suite does NOT green-light a promotion, else None.

    Promotion requires an AFFIRMATIVE GREEN - not merely 'not red'. A freshly-scaffolded all-skip suite
    (EMPTY), a missing suite (ABSENT), an unreadable/anomalous state (ERROR), and a never-run state (no file)
    all block, because none is evidence the machinery is right; deleting or never-finishing the suite was the
    trivial silent bypass this closes. ABSENT/EMPTY are excused by an explicit tests/CORRECTNESS_NA.md.
    `relaxed` (a preset that promotes stamped 'unverified'): only RED/ERROR block - a known-broken machine
    is wrong, not unverified - because an unverified promotion never claimed a green in the first place."""
    st = _read_correctness(root)
    status = str((st or {}).get("status", "")).strip().lower() if st is not None else None
    if status == "green":
        return None
    if status in ("absent", "empty", None):
        if relaxed or _has_na_waiver(root):
            return None
        which = status.upper() if status else "MISSING (run_campaign has not run its FROZEN-infra gates)"
        return (f"the correctness suite is {which} - no active checks guard the machinery, so it cannot "
                "green-light a promotion. Add >=1 real check (correctness-suite skill) and re-run "
                "run_campaign, or record an explicit N/A decision in tests/CORRECTNESS_NA.md (with a "
                "rationale) if this campaign genuinely has no simulator.")
    return (f"the correctness suite is {status.upper()} - a result built on a red/broken suite is not "
            "trustworthy. Fix the suite and re-run run_campaign before promoting.")


def _current_core_hash(root: Path | None) -> str | None:
    """Hash the FROZEN/core files on disk NOW, via the campaign's OWN frozen_core.py (the single source of
    truth for the core-file set - the guard must not fork that list). None if it cannot be determined."""
    if root is None:
        return None
    scripts = root / "scripts"
    if not (scripts / "frozen_core.py").is_file():
        return None
    try:
        if str(scripts) not in sys.path:
            sys.path.insert(0, str(scripts))
        import frozen_core  # campaign-local; existence just confirmed
        return frozen_core.core_hash(root)
    except Exception:
        return None


def green_is_stale(root: Path | None) -> bool:
    """True if the recorded correctness state is GREEN but was recorded against a DIFFERENT core than the code
    on disk now - a stale green must not gate a promotion (edit the FROZEN scorer, then promote an old
    result). Compares correctness_state.json's stored core_hash to a freshly computed one.

    Fail-SAFE: any inability to judge (no state, not green, no stored hash, frozen_core missing/unimportable,
    core unreadable) returns False. Staleness is an ADDED protection layer, so an error degrades to the
    behavior from before the check existed - it never over-blocks a legitimate promotion."""
    if root is None:
        return False
    st = _read_correctness(root)
    if st is None:
        return False
    if str(st.get("status", "")).strip().lower() != "green":
        return False                       # non-green is owned by correctness_blocks_promotion, not staleness
    recorded = st.get("core_hash")
    if not recorded:
        return False                       # an older state carries no hash -> cannot judge staleness
    current = _current_core_hash(root)
    if not current:
        return False                       # cannot hash the core now -> do not enforce
    return recorded != current


def _check_verdict(path: Path, name: str) -> str | None:
    """Deny-reason if the cited verdict artifact does not clear the gate, else None."""
    v = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    verdict = str(v.get("verdict", "")).strip().upper()
    if verdict not in PROMOTABLE:
        return (f"verdicts/{name} has verdict '{verdict or 'MISSING'}' - only CONFIRMED graduates "
                "(PROVISIONAL/QUESTIONABLE stay working results with their caveat inline)")
    tier = v.get("kill_tier")
    if tier:
        # Normalize BOTH separators. The vocabulary is unchanged -- only REFUTED and EVIDENCE_AGAINST
        # graduate -- but the kit spelled the tier three ways and only one parsed: the definition writes
        # "EVIDENCE AGAINST" (space, accepted), the guard's own docstring "EVIDENCE_AGAINST", and
        # PLANNER_PROMPT "EVIDENCE-AGAINST" (hyphen), which this check REJECTED. An agent that copied
        # the wording out of its own prompt had a legitimate kill denied over a typographic dash.
        tier_norm = str(tier).strip().upper().replace(" ", "_").replace("-", "_")
        if tier_norm not in {"REFUTED", "EVIDENCE_AGAINST"}:
            return (f"verdicts/{name} kill_tier '{tier}' cannot graduate - an INCONCLUSIVE kill "
                    "(cause unattributed) queues a fix-and-rerun unit; it does not prune")
    # `or ""` NOT `, ""`: an explicit JSON null ("refuter": null) makes .get return None, and str(None)
    # is the NON-EMPTY string "None" - which passed this check and promoted. That is exactly what a model
    # leaves behind when it copies the verdict stub without filling the field, and it was observed live
    # (a real worker promoted a current-best on refuter:null). Missing key, "", "   ",
    # null, and false must all deny; only a real id promotes.
    if not str(v.get("refuter") or "").strip():
        return (f"verdicts/{name} names no refuter - the verdict must come from an independent "
                "agent, not the generating session")
    return None


def _eid(label: str) -> str:
    """The <NN> id inside an exp label ('exp003_slug' -> '003'). A deliberate, tiny twin of the
    runner's exp_id_for: importing the runner would drag numpy and the FROZEN scorer into a hook that
    must answer in milliseconds on every file write."""
    head = str(label).strip().split("_", 1)[0]
    raw = head[3:] if head.lower().startswith("exp") else head
    return raw.zfill(3) if raw.isdigit() else raw.lower()


def promotion_subject_problem(root: Path | None, ti) -> str | None:
    """Deny-reason unless the experiment THIS WRITE PROMOTES has a promotable verdict, else None.

    Subject-matched: the written content names its experiment (RECOMMENDED.json carries its config
    path; a scoreboard token lands on its experiment's row), and the gate demands THAT experiment's
    verdict - CONFIRMED, graduating kill tier if any, named independent refuter (`_check_verdict`,
    the same bar the project-ledger surface applies). Where the campaign's verification preset owes a
    unit an independent check, that experiment carries its own verdict artifact, so an unmatched
    subject means the experiment was never verified, not that a window expired."""
    if root is None:
        return ("cannot resolve the campaign root for this write - promote from inside the campaign "
                "tree so the gate can find results/verdicts/")
    toks = {t.lower() for t in SUBJECT_RE.findall(_written_text(ti))}
    if not toks:
        return ("cannot tell WHICH experiment this write promotes - the written content names no exp "
                "id. Write the file so it names its experiment (RECOMMENDED.json carries its config "
                "path; a promotion token belongs on its experiment's scoreboard row), then the gate "
                "can match the verdict.")
    ids = {_eid(t) for t in toks}
    vdir = root / "results" / "verdicts"
    problems = []
    if vdir.is_dir():
        for p in sorted(vdir.glob("*.json")):
            try:
                v = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
            except Exception:
                continue
            subjects = {_eid(p.stem), _eid(str(v.get("exp_id", "")).strip())}
            if not (subjects & ids):
                continue
            reason = _check_verdict(p, p.name)
            if reason is None:
                return None
            problems.append(reason)
    if problems:
        return " | ".join(problems)
    return (f"no verdict artifact in results/verdicts/ matches the promoted experiment(s) "
            f"{', '.join(sorted(toks))}. A promotion needs THAT experiment's CONFIRMED verdict with a "
            "named independent refuter (hard gate #1) - run the verify skill for it (in supervised "
            "runs the driver's verification service writes it for every unit the preset owes one), "
            "then promote.")


def promotion_row_problem(root: Path | None, ti) -> str | None:
    """Deny-reason unless every promotion-time correctness check has run FOR the experiment this write
    promotes, else None.

    Under a verification preset, the expensive checks (the per-result gates, and whatever the preset
    holds back for a promotion candidate) run only after the solve of a candidate unit, and the runner
    records which experiment each ran for (results/correctness_state.json, per check: ran_for). A
    promotion of a unit those checks never ran for would be a green suite certifying nothing about the
    thing being promoted. Inactive for a legacy suite (no per-check state) and for an experiment whose
    checks artifact predates the presets (no verification.rows)."""
    if root is None:
        return None
    st = _read_correctness(root)
    checks = (st or {}).get("checks") if isinstance(st, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(checks, dict) or not checks:
        return None
    ids = {_eid(t) for t in SUBJECT_RE.findall(_written_text(ti))}
    problems = []
    for eid in sorted(ids):
        art = root / "results" / f"checks_{eid}.json"
        try:
            ck = json.loads(art.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except Exception:
            continue
        rows = ((ck.get("verification") or {}).get("rows") or {}) if isinstance(ck, dict) else {}
        if not rows:
            continue
        stale = []
        for name, e in checks.items():
            row = str(e.get("row") or "invariants")
            trig = "every" if e.get("every") else str(rows.get(row) or "every")
            gate = row == "gates" or bool(e.get("takes_arg"))
            if trig == "off" or not (gate or trig == "promotion"):
                continue
            if e.get("last_status") != "pass" or _eid(str(e.get("ran_for") or "")) != eid:
                stale.append(f"{name} (last: {e.get('last_status') or 'never'}, for "
                             f"{e.get('ran_for') or 'no experiment'})")
        if stale:
            problems.append(f"the promotion-time checks {', '.join(stale)} have not passed for exp{eid} - "
                            f"run `python scripts/run_campaign.py --run-suite due --for <exp{eid} name>` "
                            "(it records the run against that experiment), then retry")
    return " | ".join(problems) if problems else None


LABEL_RE = re.compile(r'"verification_label"\s*:\s*"([^"]*)"', re.IGNORECASE)
RELAXED_PRESETS = ("none", "minimal")


def _refuted(label: str) -> bool:
    return str(label).upper().startswith("REFUTED/") or str(label).strip().lower() == "self-refuted"


def verification_gate_problem(root: Path | None, ti) -> tuple:
    """What the promoted experiment's verification record requires of this write: (deny-reason or None,
    needs_verdict, relaxed).

    the pointer follows the true best at once, carrying the label its checks artifact holds
    (results/checks_<NN>.json `label`, machine-derived - never the guard's own reading of a preset table,
    which would be a twin). So the write must carry THAT label (RECOMMENDED.json: "verification_label";
    a scoreboard token: the label on the row) - never a stronger one - and a result a check refuted
    (`REFUTED/...`, `self-refuted`) never promotes. `relaxed` (the none / minimal presets): only a RED
    suite blocks, since such a promotion never claimed a green. An experiment whose artifact predates
    the one-check rule (no `verification.owed`) gets the established rule: its CONFIRMED verdict (needs_verdict)."""
    if root is None:
        return None, True, False
    text = _written_text(ti)
    ids = {_eid(t) for t in SUBJECT_RE.findall(text)}
    if not ids:
        return None, True, False
    problems, needs_verdict, relaxed = [], False, True
    written = [m.strip() for m in LABEL_RE.findall(text)]
    for eid in sorted(ids):
        try:
            ck = json.loads((root / "results" / f"checks_{eid}.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except Exception:
            needs_verdict, relaxed = True, False
            continue
        ver = ck.get("verification") if isinstance(ck, dict) else None
        if not isinstance(ver, dict) or "owed" not in ver:
            needs_verdict, relaxed = True, False     # predates the established verdict rule
            continue
        if str(ver.get("preset") or "") not in RELAXED_PRESETS:
            relaxed = False
        label = str(ck.get("label") or "unverified")
        if _refuted(label):
            problems.append(f"exp{eid} carries the label {label!r} - a refuted result is no one's best and "
                            "never promotes; promote the best result that was not refuted")
            continue
        if "RECOMMENDED" in str(ti.get("file_path", "")).upper():
            if not written:
                problems.append(f"exp{eid} is promoted without its label - carry \"verification_label\": "
                                f"\"{label}\" in RECOMMENDED.json (the label on its card, from "
                                f"results/checks_{eid}.json), so no reader mistakes what was checked")
            elif any(w.lower() != label.lower() for w in written):
                problems.append(f"exp{eid}'s label is {label!r} (results/checks_{eid}.json), but the write says "
                                f"{', '.join(repr(w) for w in written)} - carry exactly the label on its card")
        elif label.upper() not in text.upper():
            problems.append(f"exp{eid} is promoted on the scoreboard without its label {label!r} on the row")
    return (" | ".join(problems) if problems else None), needs_verdict, (relaxed and not needs_verdict)


def contest_problem(root: Path | None, ti) -> str | None:
    """Deny-reason while the promoted experiment's gate outcome is CONTESTED and undecided, else None.

    A worker that disputes a gate outcome files results/contests/<stem>.json through `--record` and does
    not decide it: the driver's independent verifier does, and the driver itself moves the pointer when a
    contested pass stands (the runner's _contest_resolve). Until that verdict lands the pointer waits -
    a promotion write for the contested experiment, by the worker that filed the contest or the next one,
    is refused by name. A resolved contest no longer blocks: the label rule above decides."""
    if root is None:
        return None
    cdir = root / "results" / "contests"
    if not cdir.is_dir():
        return None
    ids = {_eid(t) for t in SUBJECT_RE.findall(_written_text(ti))}
    if not ids:
        return None
    for p in sorted(cdir.glob("*.json")):
        try:
            c = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except Exception:
            continue
        if not isinstance(c, dict):
            continue
        subjects = {_eid(p.stem), _eid(str(c.get("exp") or "")), _eid(str(c.get("exp_id") or ""))}
        if not (subjects & ids):
            continue
        if str(c.get("status") or "pending") == "pending":
            return (f"{p.stem}'s gate outcome ({c.get('disputes') or 'pass'}) is CONTESTED and undecided "
                    f"(results/contests/{p.name}) - the pointer waits for the driver's independent verifier; "
                    "the recorded outcome stands unless the verdict is REFUTED, and a contested pass that "
                    "stands is promoted by the driver, not by a worker")
    return None


def scoreboard_promotion(ti) -> bool:
    """True if this write INTRODUCES a `CONFIRMED` / `NEW BEST` token into the scoreboard."""
    if "scoreboard" not in str(ti.get("file_path", "")).lower():
        return False
    for new, old in _edit_chunks(ti):
        for tok in ("CONFIRMED", "NEW BEST"):
            if tok in new and tok not in old:
                return True
    return False


def main():
    try:
        data = json.load(sys.stdin)
        tool_name = data.get("tool_name", "")
        ti = data.get("tool_input") or {}
        fp_str = str(ti.get("file_path", ""))
    except Exception:
        _note_bypass(None, "could not parse hook stdin")
        _allow()
        return
    if tool_name not in ("Write", "Edit", "MultiEdit"):
        _allow()
        return
    fp = Path(fp_str) if fp_str else None
    root = _campaign_root(fp) if fp else None
    global _LOG_ROOT
    _LOG_ROOT = root

    # ---- surface 0: configs/loop.json - the metric_revision dial (attended-session-only, fail-open-
    #      logged) and the campaign.metric_epochs record (append-only, evidence-checked, FAIL-CLOSED) ----
    if _is_loop_config(fp):
        try:
            problem = config_dial_problem(fp, ti)
        except Exception as exc:
            _note_bypass(root, f"config-dial guard error: {exc}")
            problem = None
        if problem:
            _deny(problem)
        try:
            problem = epoch_block_problem(root, fp, ti)
        except Exception as exc:
            problem = f"could not validate campaign.metric_epochs ({exc})"
        if problem:
            _deny("epoch gate: " + problem)
        _allow()
        return

    # ---- surface 1: the PROJECT ledger <project>/DISCOVERIES.md - subject-matched, FAIL-CLOSED ----
    if _is_project_ledger(fp):
        try:
            refs = sorted(set(VERDICT_REF_RE.findall(_written_text(ti))))
            if not refs:
                _deny("project-ledger gate: the entry cites no verdict artifact. Promoting a finding to "
                      "the project DISCOVERIES ledger requires citing the SOURCE campaign's verdict by "
                      "path (campaigns/<slug>/results/verdicts/<id>.json) - run the verify skill in that "
                      "campaign, get CONFIRMED, then cite the file. CLAUDE.md hard gate #1.")
                return
            problems = []
            for name in refs:
                found = _find_project_verdict(fp.parent, name)
                if found is None:
                    problems.append(f"cited verdict artifact not found under campaigns/**/verdicts/: {name}")
                    continue
                reason = _check_verdict(found, name)
                if reason:
                    problems.append(reason)
                    continue
                src_root = found.parent.parent.parent   # <campaign>/results/verdicts/<file>
                suite_reason = correctness_blocks_promotion(src_root)
                if suite_reason:
                    problems.append(f"source campaign '{src_root.name}': {suite_reason}")
                elif green_is_stale(src_root):
                    problems.append(f"source campaign '{src_root.name}': its correctness green was "
                                    "recorded against a DIFFERENT version of its FROZEN/core code than "
                                    "what is on disk now - re-run its suite before promoting the finding "
                                    "upward")
            if problems:
                _deny("project-ledger gate: " + " | ".join(problems))
                return
            _allow()
        except Exception as exc:
            _deny(f"project-ledger gate (fail-closed): could not validate the promotion ({exc}). Fix the "
                  "verdict citation or the guard input and retry; the project ledger is the record that "
                  "survives fork-and-archive - the one unrecoverable write.")
        return

    # ---- surface 2: RECOMMENDED / scoreboard-token writes - recency-checked, FAIL-OPEN-LOGGED ----
    try:
        is_promo = "RECOMMENDED" in fp_str.upper() or scoreboard_promotion(ti)
        if not is_promo:
            _allow()
            return
        # The promoted experiment's own checks artifact decides what this promotion needs: its
        # honest label, carried in the write; no refuted result; under none / minimal only a RED suite
        # blocks. An artifact from before the one-check rule keeps the established rule (its CONFIRMED verdict).
        gate_reason, needs_verdict, relaxed = verification_gate_problem(root, ti)
        suite_reason = correctness_blocks_promotion(root, relaxed=relaxed)
        if suite_reason:
            _deny("promotion gate: " + suite_reason)
            return
        if green_is_stale(root):
            _deny("promotion gate: the correctness suite's green was recorded against a DIFFERENT version of "
                  "the FROZEN/core code than what is on disk now (scripts/frozen_core.py) - re-run the suite "
                  "(run_campaign) so it validates the current core before marking a current-best.")
            return
        epoch_reason = epoch_blocks_promotion(root)
        if epoch_reason:
            _deny("promotion gate: " + epoch_reason)
            return
        row_reason = promotion_row_problem(root, ti)
        if row_reason:
            _deny("promotion gate: " + row_reason)
            return
        contest_reason = contest_problem(root, ti)
        if contest_reason:
            _deny("promotion gate: " + contest_reason)
            return
        if gate_reason:
            _deny("promotion gate: " + gate_reason)
            return
        if not needs_verdict:
            _allow()          # promoted at once with its honest label
            return
        subject_problem = promotion_subject_problem(root, ti)
        if subject_problem is None:
            _allow()
            return
        _deny("promotion gate: " + subject_problem)
    except Exception as exc:
        _note_bypass(root, f"promotion-surface guard error: {exc}")
        _allow()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
